 "floorplan_why": "781.92 x 172.8 (height = the E face left under the 151.2-um link bridge on the 43.2-um child lattice). 8 macros = 49.0k um2, std ~18.5k um2 (vmx_w 7.1k + vmx_r 10.5k + hep 0.85k), overall utilisation ~52 %. Flow E -> W for reads: 1,026 response pins (E) -> response-queue macros (3 columns x 2 rows at x 429.8 / 546.5 / 663.1, write data in from the E pins, rd_out on their W faces) -> queue output buffer + slow -> fast ratio FIFO in the 44-um band at x 387..432 and in the macro channels -> staging macros (x 22.5 and 216, rd_out W) -> vm_rq flops at the W pins. Writes W -> E: WFC pins (W) -> pre-queue / fast -> slow FIFO in the 73-um band above the staging macros -> write skid / link register -> E pins. HEP macro (generated 512 x 64, 96.6 x 29.7) in the sixth queue slot at the E pins. >= 20 um channels around every macro; E pin strip 24 um; no pins on N; the 782-um span is forced by the macro row under a 172.8-um face (two 171-um staging macros + three 95-um queue columns + channels), measured by the --cts gate. Cut W-E through the tile at the staging macros: 527 b write + 1,032 b read over 73 um of free M2 / M4 height (2 x 1,520 tracks) -> 0.51."
